":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; creates no separate obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies launch history, the earlier circular and the new-product and post-authorisation/registration context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Explains the parallel run and acceptance through existing channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading for extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Monitoring and feedback explain the extension; impose no submission condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends the parallel run through 29 November 2024; enhancements explain that extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Repeats the mandatory route, describes reporting integration and permits annual-fee payment through e-IP.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading creates no selected-control obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Practicability qualifies SFC operational enhancements; contact guidance does not qualify the submission mandate.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Division attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Commission attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"End marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Footnote identifies the product categories associated with the scope clause.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Defines WINGS; does not establish a separate submission route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control concerns persons making applications or submissions for investment products administered by IPD, rather than all activities of an institution or all industry participants. It encompasses new-product and post-authorisation/registration submissions; specified reporting requests are to be integrated.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Footnote 1 supplies product categories. WINGS means Web-based INteGrated Service and hosts e-IP. The packet does not supply detailed classification rules for borderline products or communications.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u17","u18"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception or grandfathering is stated. 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not to compulsory submission.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'must' establishes the submission-route requirement. 'can also' makes annual-fee payment through e-IP an optional facility. Statements about future enhancements and integration do not themselves impose additional user duties.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The original 29 October 2024 endpoint is extended to 29 November 2024. Mandatory routing begins on 30 November 2024, inclusively. The packet does not specify dispatch-versus-receipt timing or treatment of follow-up material in existing cases.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 launch circular is referenced but absent. The listed external-authorities dependency contains no substantive text. Operational classification and legacy-case details cannot be resolved from those unavailable materials; the express transition date is not conditioned on their contents or completion of enhancements.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the referenced 8 July 2024 circular specify how follow-up submissions in cases opened before 30 November 2024 must be routed?","Which event determines the submission date for material dispatched before, but received on or after, 30 November 2024?","What classification guidance determines whether a borderline communication is an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered product?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The control is evaluated for one identified application or submission, not for whole-institution compliance.","Extending the parallel run extends its existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.","The supplied submission date is established under the applicable timing convention; this packet does not define that convention.","Product and communication classification is supplied with professional judgment where needed."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"processing new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.","unit_id":"u3"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"2 Web-based INteGrated Service.","unit_id":"u18"}],"distinction":"The express text supports one mandatory-route reading, without a sufficiently grounded rival that postpones the date, exempts existing cases or makes annual-fee payment compulsory. A covered submission made through an existing non-e-IP channel on 29 November 2024 falls within the extended parallel run; the same submission on 30 November falls within the compulsory e-IP control and fails that route check. A fee payment alone does not become a covered submission merely because e-IP can process it. The strongest uncertainty concerns operational treatment of legacy-case follow-ups and the event fixing the submission date.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The identified item is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, interpreted with the product categories in footnote 1. Optional fee payment alone does not establish this classification.","name":"covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The Gregorian date on which the identified application or submission is treated as submitted under the applicable timing convention. Dispatch-versus-receipt treatment is not specified in the packet.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u4","u7","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The identified application or submission was submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_e_ip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_e_ip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["For a case initiated through an existing channel before the transition, is later correspondence itself a covered submission requiring e-IP?","Does unavailable operational guidance distinguish attempted transmission from accepted receipt when determining the submission date?"],"statement":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route from 30 November 2024. For each covered application or submission made from that date, submission to IPD must use e-IP. The extended parallel run permits existing channels through 29 November 2024. Enhancement plans do not make the transition conditional, and the annual-fee facility remains optional. The formal result tests only routing when its scope holds; an out-of-scope item receives no compliance verdict from this control.","subject":"Routing of applications and submissions for IPD-administered investment products"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the extended parallel run and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; no independent condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Provides launch history, WINGS context and examples of application/submission types; the earlier circular is not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the parallel run, read with its extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback; adds no submission condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Confirms the revised parallel-run endpoint; enhancement rationale does not expressly condition commencement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the compulsory-route context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the compulsory route, describes integration of reporting requests and separately permits fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading; no independent route requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Operational review and contact guidance; practicability qualifies enhancements, not compulsory submission.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing commission.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Document-end marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope; exhaustiveness remains unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not create a separate route obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD and submitted to IPD. It governs the submitting actor in that capacity; it does not impose an institution-wide or bank-specific duty.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"IPD and e-IP are identified, and WINGS is expanded. The footnote lists product categories without expressly saying whether the list exhausts IPD-administered products. Applications and submissions are not comprehensively defined.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel run, whose endpoint is extended. No post-transition exception or grandfathering rule is stated. The practicability qualification concerns operational enhancement.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"Must establishes the compulsory submission route. Can also makes annual-fee settlement an available facility. Statements that features will be introduced and requests will be integrated do not themselves create new reporting or payment duties.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The revised parallel run ends on 29 November 2024 and the compulsory route begins on 30 November 2024, inclusively. The original 29 October endpoint is superseded. Treatment of later correspondence in pre-transition cases is not expressly addressed.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The earlier launch circular and the packet's external-authorities.24ec50 dependency are unavailable. They may clarify product classification, existing channels and migration procedures. The supplied text states a fixed commencement date without making it contingent on enhancement completion.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Is the product list in footnote 1 exhaustive, or does IPD administration independently determine coverage?","Does the earlier circular provide special handling for follow-up submissions in cases opened through existing channels before 30 November 2024?","What do the unavailable launch circular and external-authorities.24ec50 dependency specify about submission classification and migration procedures?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified submission event, not whole-institution compliance or whether an underlying filing is due.","Extending the parallel run carries forward its existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.","The event's submission date determines application of the compulsory route; no unstated grandfathering exception is inserted.","Product and submission classification remain supplied facts requiring judgment where the retained text is insufficient."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"}],"distinction":"This reading applies the transition to each covered submission event, including later submissions relating to an earlier case where they otherwise qualify. It preserves optional fee settlement and treats enhancement completion as rationale rather than a commencement condition. The strongest uncertainty is whether unavailable migration provisions qualify the treatment of existing cases; the retained text supplies insufficient support for a separate grandfathering reading.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD. Classification takes account of footnote 1 and does not classify use of the optional annual-fee facility alone as a covered submission.","name":"covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made to IPD.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["For an existing case, which later communications count as applications or submissions subject to the new route?","Does missing migration guidance provide any express exception to the event-date reading?"],"statement":"For each covered application or submission made to IPD on or after 30 November 2024, the submitting actor must use e-IP. Existing channels remain accepted during the extended parallel run through 29 November 2024. The identified reporting requests fall within the integration described by the circular, without this text independently establishing when reports are due. Annual-fee settlement through e-IP remains optional. Within the formal scope, a true result means that this submission satisfies the selected route control; outside that scope, the formalization makes no compliance determination.","subject":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route and transition date"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Establishes the extended parallel run and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; no independent duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies the launch, WINGS platform, submission types and earlier circular; the earlier circular is not supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Explains parallel running as continued acceptance of existing submission channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Heading for extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Reports monitoring and industry engagement; imposes no submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Confirms extension to 29 November 2024; planned enhancements explain the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Heading supporting the full-adoption context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the mandatory route, identifies integrated reporting and separately permits annual-fee payment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Operational review statement and contact invitation; the practicability qualification concerns SFC enhancements.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Closing marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope; exhaustiveness is unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS without adding a separate route requirement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The requirement attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD. It applies to persons making those submissions, without identifying a particular regulated actor class or creating a general duty to submit.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is the investment-product application/submission system on WINGS, whose expansion is supplied. Footnote 1 lists product categories but does not expressly state whether the list exhaustively defines IPD-administered products.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception is stated. The phrase 'where practicable' qualifies SFC review and enhancement, not the compulsory submission route.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' establishes the compulsory route. Integration and enhancements are announced system changes. 'Can also' describes an optional annual-fee payment facility; the enquiry invitation adds no mandatory filing step.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The 29 July 2024 launch and original 29 October 2024 parallel-run endpoint are historical context. The extension carries parallel running through 29 November 2024, with compulsory e-IP use beginning on 30 November 2024. No express grandfathering rule for pending matters is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 circular and external-authorities.24ec50 dependency are not supplied. Their possible definitions, procedural conditions or exceptions cannot be resolved. Integration of existing IP E-submission requests does not itself establish the underlying reporting triggers or deadlines.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively define the covered products, or identify categories within the broader class of products administered by IPD?","Does the 8 July 2024 circular or the unavailable external dependency specify exceptions, outage arrangements or treatment of submissions in matters initiated before 30 November 2024?","Which existing IP E-submission requests qualify as covered submissions, and what separate sources establish their reporting triggers and deadlines?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Extending the parallel run extends its stated feature of accepting existing channels through 29 November 2024.","The transition applies by the date of each submission event; the supplied text provides no exemption based on when the underlying matter began.","Whether a particular product and communication fall within the IPD submission scope must be established separately; unknown classifications remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit t